%U A400705 3,1,5,1,2,2,5,1,2,2,9,1,2,2,3,1,3,1,4,1,2,2,1,10,1,2,2,3,1,3,1,4,1,2,4,1,2,2,1,11,1,2,2,3
%N A400705 A version of the building sequence A400000 for positive- and negative-integer numbered plots: this sequence gives the heights of the buildings at negative-numbered plots, in order.
%C A400705 In A400000 the buildings are erected on a semi-infinite row of plots numbered with the positive integers 1, 2, 3, 4, ... In the present sequence the buildings are erected along an infinite row of plots labeled with the integers, in order, at lots 0, 1, -1, 2, -2, 3, -3, ..., using the same rule as in A400000.
%C A400705 This sequence shows the heights of the buildings at plots 0, -1, -2, -3, -4, ...
%C A400705 The central group of buildings, in plots ..., -6, -5, -3, ..., -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, ..., 6, ... have heights ..., 1, 2, 1, 4, 1, 2, 0, 1, 3, 1, 2, 1, 6, ... The heights at plots 0, -1, -2, ... form the present sequence, and the heights at plots 0, 1, 2, ... form A400706. For reasons of symmetry, the central building of height 0 appears in both sequences. - _N. J. A. Sloane_, Oct 24 2026
%H A400705 Scott R. Shannon, <a href="/A400705/b400705.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
